  "verdict": "H0 / ARTIFACT: the apparent positive lead is NOT robust - it collapses monotonically as the momentum-drawdown is deepened (see robustness.lead_median_by_drawdown; not significant at the genuine-rollover end frac=0.75), the theta=0.3 feasibility headroom is ~0 (3rd-earliest region peaks at median 0), and the national-only control LAGS - so the 'lead' is a regional-NOISE artifact (the loose 50% drawdown fires early on noisy regional momenta during the rise, e.g. at ~1.5% ILI in November), NOT a genuine spatial signal. The spatial-curvature hypothesis H1 is NOT supported (honest negative, with E6)."
